        "IQS_05": {
            "question_id": "IQS_05",
            "status": "scored",
            "score": 9,
            "description": "Within its clearly defined business scope (enterprise productivity, cloud infrastructure, AI integration), Microsoft has multiple layers of competitive advantage with strong, documented evidence that competitors cannot easily replicate at reasonable cost:\n\n1. Enterprise Switching Costs (Strongest Moat, Verified): Microsoft 365 has 400M+ paid commercial seats. Switching costs for a 10,000-employee enterprise are estimated at $50-100M direct costs + 12-24 months disruption. Customer retention exceeds 95%, with annual price increases of 3-7% absorbed without meaningful churn. Active Directory/Entra ID manages authentication for ~95% of Fortune 500, making identity layer a deep lock-in.\n\n2. Azure Cloud Infrastructure + Hybrid Lock-In (Verified): ~25% global cloud share, growing 30%+/year with $75B+ FY2025 revenue. Azure Arc enables hybrid management where AWS/GCP are demonstrably weaker. Azure Hybrid Benefit provides ~40% IaaS discount for existing license holders - structural cost incentive.\n\n4. Copilot Network (Verified but Evolving): Copilot for M365 at $30/user/month, with rapid commercial adoption. AI contributed ~half of Azure's recent growth. Exclusive OpenAI partnership (49% stake, $13B+ invested) provides GPT model access competitors cannot replicate. Data flywheel: Copilot's value increases with M365 workflow data depth.\n\nEvidence is concrete, multi-source corroborated, and quantifies replication costs ($M-$100M per enterprise migration, $50B+ capex to match Azure, multi-year migration timelines). However, key limitations apply: (a) OpenAI partnership exclusivity is at risk (governance instability noted as critical threat); (b) regulatory pressure (EU DMA) may force unbundling of Teams/Office; (c) FY26 capex of $190B is pressuring margins (gross margin compressed to 67.6%); (d) AI moat durability threatened by open-source models and competitor cloud growth (AWS still leads at 30-32%). Score of 9 reflects very strong, well-documented evidence of durable advantage that competitors cannot easily replicate at reasonable cost, with minor deductions for emerging risks.",
